{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. You’re here because of nausea and vomiting again, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. It came on suddenly yesterday—white, mucus-like vomit. I tried my usual meds: Tigan through the J-tube, Ativan and Amerol by mouth, but nothing helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were just discharged a few days ago for a similar episode, and you felt okay for about two days at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was eating solids and felt much better. Then this hit out of nowhere. No diarrhea this time, just the nausea and vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that fits with your history of gastroparesis flares. Your labs show your potassium is low—3.0—which we expect with vomiting. We’ve started IV fluids and 40 mEq of potassium to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that makes sense. I’ve been so nauseous I haven’t been able to keep anything down. Is that why I feel so weak?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, low potassium can cause weakness and fatigue. We’re correcting it now. For the nausea, we’re giving IV morphine and Ativan—same combo that helped last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good, that usually works best for me. I just wish we knew why this keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t have a clear cause for your gastroparesis, but we know this treatment plan helps. For now, we’ll keep you on bowel rest—no food by mouth—for a day or two to let your stomach settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. But how will I get nutrition?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue using your J-tube for hydration and meds. We’re not feeding through it yet, just keeping it clear. Once you’re stable, we’ll slowly restart oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds—like thyroid and omeprazole—should I still take those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your levothyroxine and switch you to IV pantoprazole for now, since you’re not eating. We’ll go back to omeprazole when you can take pills again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve also been anxious—this whole cycle is so frustrating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-03-13 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I completely understand. We’ll keep your lorazepam available for nausea and anxiety. We’re also continuing your citalopram for depression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-03-14 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your potassium is up to 3.6 this morning—much better. How’s the nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-03-14 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much improved. I haven’t vomited since last night, and the nausea is mild now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-03-14 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re going to start you on clear liquids—water, broth, apple juice—and see how you tolerate it. Small sips, every 15 minutes at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-03-14 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try. Should I still take my Tigan or dronabinol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-03-14 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hold off on those for now. We’ll use them only if nausea returns. We’ve also switched your Ativan to oral form since you’re keeping things down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-03-14 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well—no vomiting, and you’ve kept down the clear liquids. We’re going to advance you to a soft diet: applesauce, mashed potatoes, yogurt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-03-14 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. Can I have toast or crackers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-03-14 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, small amounts. But avoid fatty, spicy, or fibrous foods. We also talked about a 'small particle diet'—finely blended foods that are easier to digest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-03-14 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard of that. Do you think it could help me avoid these flares?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-03-14 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might. Some patients with gastroparesis do better on it. We’ll discuss it more with your gastroenterologist at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-03-14 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve eaten the soft foods and feel okay. No nausea at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-03-14 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll keep you on the soft diet tonight and aim for regular solids tomorrow if you continue to do well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You made it through the night without issues. We’re going to try a regular diet—small portions, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m ready to go home. When do you think I can be discharged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you tolerate today’s meals and stay stable, we can likely discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Should I restart all my home meds when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly as before: levothyroxine at night, omeprazole, Tigan and dronabinol as needed for nausea, and your vitamin D twice a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And lorazepam for anxiety or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-03-15 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 0.5 to 1 mg every six hours as needed. But try to use it only when necessary, especially for anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-03-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well—ate a full meal, no nausea, vitals stable. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow around noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-03-15 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. Do I need to follow up with my gastroenterologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-03-15 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you have an appointment with Dr. Evans in a week. They’ll review your progress and possibly adjust your plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-03-15 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the radiology appointment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-03-15 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have a scan scheduled next week—likely a follow-up on your hiatal hernia, though it’s small and probably not causing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Final check—you’re still feeling well, no nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No nausea at all. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Remember: advance your diet slowly, stick to smaller meals, and consider the small particle diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And call if the nausea comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Use your PRN meds first, but if vomiting persists, come back to the ED. Otherwise, see Dr. Evans next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we hope this flare stays resolved. Your husband is on his way up, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, he’ll be here in 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-03-16 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll have the nurse go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just to confirm—I’m to continue all my usual meds, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly as before. No changes unless Dr. Evans recommends them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the J-tube—just for meds if needed, not for feeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. Use it only if you can’t swallow pills or need hydration during a flare. Keep the site clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-03-16 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Take it easy at home, and we’ll see you only if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-03-16 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge orders are signed. You can leave once your husband arrives and the nurse reviews your instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-03-16 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m so glad to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-03-16 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick final check—still feeling well?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-03-16 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no issues at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-03-16 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Discharge is official. Take care, and we hope to not see you back soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-03-16 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’ll follow up with Dr. Evans and take it slow at home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-03-13 19:47:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-03-16 14:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis, J-tube placement, and Nissen fundoplication was readmitted for recurrent nausea and vomiting just days after a prior discharge for a similar flare. She presented with sudden-onset nausea and mucinous emesis, failed outpatient management with Tigan, Ativan, and Amerol, and was found to have hypokalemia (K 3.0) likely due to vomiting. She was managed with bowel rest, IV fluids, IV potassium replacement, and a combination of IV morphine and lorazepam, which resolved her symptoms. She gradually advanced from clear liquids to a soft diet and then to solid foods without complications. Her potassium normalized, and she was discharged home in stable condition. She was counseled on a small particle diet, instructed to continue her home medications, and advised to follow up with her gastroenterologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Attention to gastrostomy",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Diaphragmatic hernia without mention of obstruction or gangrene",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Intestinal disaccharidase deficiencies and disaccharide malabsorption",
      "Adhesive capsulitis of shoulder",
      "Unspecified vitamin D deficiency",
      "Personal history of other malignant neoplasm of skin"
    ]
  }
}
